This is the real latency cost of acks=all: a write is only as fast as the slowest in-sync replica.
There’s no rule that you need as many brokers as partitions. One broker can hold hundreds of partitions.

Kafka brokers are not interchangeable. Each one has its own identity, its own data, and an address other brokers and clients remember. A StatefulSet gives you exactly those three things.


Every time a pod started, it downloaded confluent-kafka from PyPI, and on a slow connection the download timed out. pip failed, the container exited, and Kubernetes restarted it.

